{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the screen's frozen again. One moment. Right, go on, what's happened?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ankle. Twisted it yesterday. Football.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Which ankle? It just refreshed, say it again.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Left. It's fat and it hurts. I'm tired.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. You walked in, so you can take your weight on it?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, with pain. Can we just...",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hang on. The walking bit again, I missed it.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): I can walk. It hurts when I do.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Did you hear a crack or a pop when it went?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Toes numb, or pins and needles?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is the knee sore as well?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Your notes say asthma. Is that still going?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Umm, years. Blue inhaler, salbutermol, couple of times a week.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any cough with the asthma?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. At night.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever since yesterday?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Coach had a go, boot was soaked, I don't even...",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No fever.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Lost any weight lately?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. Are you even listening?",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, inbox popped up. Any chest pain, ever?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): I can see swelling over the outside of the left ankle. Back of the outside bone, is that the worst bit?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No. It's the soft bit at the front. Ow.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): I felt the inside bone, not tender, and the outside bone wasn't your sore spot. Ottawa rules, tender malleolus or unable to walk four steps means an x-ray, so not today. Could be the ligament or a small chip, but I will not conclude a fracture. Working impression is a lateral ankle sprain.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): So I can play Saturday?",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): No football till it's settled. Rest it, keep it elevated, ice in a tea towel. Paracetamol two hundred and fifty milligrams by mouth, up to four times a day, for the pain. Any allergies?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): if it's not settled in a week, come back and see me. if you can't bear weight on it, we'll arrange an ankle x-ray."
 ],
